  "body": "Using ART 1.25.9 in Windows 11 Pro. When I load a file in the ART GUI editor and go to rename a file via the menu that is pulled up via `F2`, I get a message that says \"Failed to rename file\". I have noticed that I can right-click and rename a file from the preview bar _if_ I have not yet clicked to load said file into the main editor window.\n\nSimilarly, whichever files I have loaded into the editor window while ART has been open I cannot delete in Windows Explorer as it reports them all are open in ART. In previous versions, I could delete any files which were or had been opened in the ART editor. Only closing ART completely releases the files.",
